1	//! Assembly + the BC-3 self-gate oracle (AWL-BC-IR.md §11.5). Lowers every MIR
2	//! function (flow or shell) to a [`Body`], emits the module-wide instruction
3	//! stream, builds a `ParsedModule` (chunk set / order owned by the encoder),
4	//! encodes to `.beam` bytes, and re-loads + `validate_module`s the result
5	//! through the loader's five layers — a rejection is a hard error, never a
6	//! silent artifact.
7	
8	use beamr::atom::{Atom, AtomTable};
9	use beamr::loader::encode::encode_module;
10	use beamr::loader::load::{ParsedModule, resolve_imports};
11	use beamr::loader::validate::validate_module;
12	use beamr::loader::{ExportEntry, load_beam_chunks};
